# {{projectName}} - Development Instructions for GitHub Copilot

You are working on a NestJS application that uses:
- **API**: {{#if isGraphQL}}GraphQL with Apollo Server{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}REST API with Swagger{{/if}}
- **Database**: {{#if isMongoose}}MongoDB with Mongoose{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}}{{#if_eq database 'postgresql'}}PostgreSQL{{/if_eq}}{{#if_eq database 'mysql'}}MySQL{{/if_eq}} with Prisma{{/if}}
- **Additional Services**: {{#if hasRedis}}Redis{{/if}}{{#if hasElasticsearch}}{{#if hasRedis}}, {{/if}}Elasticsearch{{/if}}{{#if hasRabbitmq}}{{#if hasRedis}}{{#if hasElasticsearch}}, {{/if}}, {{else}}{{#if hasElasticsearch}}, {{/if}}{{/if}}RabbitMQ{{/if}}

## Code Generation Guidelines

### Module Structure
When creating new feature modules, use this structure:
```
src/entity/
├── entity.module.ts
{{#if isGraphQL}}├── entity.resolver.ts{{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}├── entity.controller.ts{{/if}}
├── entity.service.ts
{{#if isMongoose}}├── entity.repository.ts
├── entity.schema.ts{{/if}}
{{#if isGraphQL}}├── inputs/entity-*.input.ts
├── objects/entity.object.ts{{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}├── dto/entity-*.dto.ts{{/if}}
└── errors/entity-*.error.ts
```

### File Naming
- Use entity name as prefix: `user.service.ts`, `user.module.ts`
- {{#if isGraphQL}}GraphQL: `*.object.ts` for outputs, `*.input.ts` for inputs{{/if}}
- {{#if isRest}}REST: `*.dto.ts` for data transfer objects{{/if}}
- Errors: `entity-specific.error.ts`

{{#if isGraphQL}}
### GraphQL Patterns

**Resolvers:**
- Queries: `entity` (single), `entities` (plural)
- Mutations: `entityCreate`, `entityUpdate`, `entityDelete`
- Always use constants from `src/common/common.constraints.ts`:

```typescript
import { INPUT_KEY, INPUT_SORT, INPUT_PAGINATION } from '../../common/common.constraints';

@Query(() => EntityObject)
async entity(@Args(INPUT_KEY) input: EntityInput): Promise<EntityObject> {
  // implementation
}

@Query(() => EntityPaginationResponse)
async entities(
  @Args(INPUT_KEY) input: EntityFindManyInput,
  @Args(INPUT_SORT) sort: EntityFindManySortInput,
  @Args(INPUT_PAGINATION) pagination: PaginationInput,
): Promise<EntityPaginationResponse> {
  // implementation
}
```

**Input Types:**
```typescript
@InputType()
export class EntityCreateInput {
{{#if isMongoose}}  @Field(() => GraphQLObjectID, { nullable: true })
  id?: string;{{/if}}
  
  @Field()
  name: string;
}
```

**Object Types:**
```typescript
@ObjectType()
export class EntityObject {
{{#if isMongoose}}  constructor(input: EntityDocument | EntityObject) {
    Object.assign(this, {
      ...((input as any)._doc
        ? (input as EntityDocument).toObject({ virtuals: true })
        : input),
    });
  }{{/if}}

  @Field(() => ID)
  id: string;

  @Field()
  name: string;
}
```
{{/if}}

{{#if isRest}}
### REST API Patterns

**Controllers:**
```typescript
@Controller('entities')
@ApiTags('entities')
export class EntityController {
  constructor(private readonly entityService: EntityService) {}

  @Get()
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Get all entities' })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 200, type: [EntityResponseDto] })
  async findAll(): Promise<EntityResponseDto[]> {
    return this.entityService.findAll();
  }

  @Post()
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Create entity' })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 201, type: EntityResponseDto })
  async create(@Body() createDto: CreateEntityDto): Promise<EntityResponseDto> {
    return this.entityService.create(createDto);
  }
}
```

**DTOs:**
```typescript
export class CreateEntityDto {
  @ApiProperty({ description: 'Entity name', example: 'Example' })
  @IsString()
  @MinLength(2)
  name: string;
}

export class EntityResponseDto {
  @ApiProperty()
  id: string;

  @ApiProperty()
  name: string;
}
```
{{/if}}

### Error Handling
Always extend base error classes and never use them directly:

```typescript
import { NotFoundError } from '../../common/errors/business.error';

export const ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_CODE = 'ENTITY_NOT_FOUND';

export class EntityNotFoundError extends NotFoundError {
  constructor() {
    super('Entity not found', ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_CODE);
  }
}
```

{{#if isGraphQL}}Register errors in `src/utils/registerEnums.ts`:
```typescript
export const Errors = {
  ...GqlCommonErrors,
  ...GqlEntityErrors,
};
```{{/if}}

{{#if isMongoose}}
### MongoDB/Mongoose Patterns

**Schemas:**
```typescript
@Schema()
export class Entity {
  @Prop({ required: true })
  name: string;

  @Prop({ default: Date.now })
  createdAt: Date;
}

export type EntityDocument = Entity & Document;
export const EntitySchema = SchemaFactory.createForClass(Entity);
```

**Repositories:**
```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityRepository {
  constructor(
    @InjectModel(Entity.name) private readonly entityModel: Model<EntityDocument>,
  ) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<EntityDocument | null> {
    return this.entityModel.findById(id).exec();
  }

  async create(data: any): Promise<EntityDocument> {
    const entity = new this.entityModel(data);
    return entity.save();
  }
}
```

Register schemas in `src/common/modules/app-mongoose-models.module.ts`.
{{/if}}

{{#if isPrisma}}
### Prisma Patterns

**Service with Prisma:**
```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityService {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<Entity | null> {
    return this.prisma.entity.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  }

  async create(data: Prisma.EntityCreateInput): Promise<Entity> {
    return this.prisma.entity.create({ data });
  }

  async update(id: string, data: Prisma.EntityUpdateInput): Promise<Entity> {
    return this.prisma.entity.update({ where: { id }, data });
  }
}
```

Use proper Prisma types: `Entity`, `Prisma.EntityCreateInput`, etc.
{{/if}}

### Service Layer
- Handle business logic only
{{#if isMongoose}}- Delegate database operations to repositories{{/if}}
{{#if isPrisma}}- Use PrismaService for database operations{{/if}}
- Always validate inputs and throw appropriate errors
- Keep services stateless

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityService {
  constructor(
    {{#if isMongoose}}private readonly entityRepository: EntityRepository,{{/if}}
    {{#if isPrisma}}private readonly prisma: PrismaService,{{/if}}
  ) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<{{#if isGraphQL}}EntityObject{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}EntityResponseDto{{/if}}> {
    {{#if isMongoose}}const entity = await this.entityRepository.findById(id);{{/if}}
    {{#if isPrisma}}const entity = await this.prisma.entity.findUnique({ where: { id } });{{/if}}
    
    if (!entity) {
      throw new EntityNotFoundError();
    }

    return {{#if isGraphQL}}new EntityObject(entity){{/if}}{{#if isRest}}entity{{/if}};
  }
}
```

